  "id": "mood-congruent",
  "term": "mood congruent",
  "definition": "Mood congruent describes a match between a person’s current mood and the emotional information they attend to, such as sadness being linked with greater attention to sad faces. In this context, it refers to a mood-specific bias toward material with the same emotional tone as the mood.",
